        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(infra): bound response body read in readResponseBodySnippet non-streaming fallback",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n**Problem:** `readResponseBodySnippet()` non-streaming fallback (`!body.getReader`) calls `response.text()` without any size bound, buffering the entire response before the `maxBytes` check runs.\n\n**Solution:** Replace `response.text()` with `readResponsePrefix(response, maxBytes)` which caps the read at `maxBytes` bytes regardless of path.\n\n**What changed:** `readResponsePrefix` exported from `http-body.ts` (was private). Non-streaming fallback in `http-error-body.ts` uses it instead of `response.text()`. Test mock updated to include `arrayBuffer()`.\n\n**What did NOT change:** Streaming path behavior (already bounded). Return type/API surface of `readResponseBodySnippet`. Any caller behavior -- all callers pass the same limits.\n\nFixes #101269\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n**Behavior addressed:** Non-streaming fallback now reads at most `maxBytes` bytes instead of the entire response body.\n\n**Real environment tested:** Linux x64 (kernel 4.19.112), Node.js v24.13.1, OpenClaw commit 50f4f9db9a (PR head)\n\n**After-fix evidence:**\n\n9/9 unit tests pass including both streaming and body-less paths:\n```\n ✓ readResponseBodySnippet > returns full text when under both limits (body-less path)\n ✓ readResponseBodySnippet > truncates by maxChars when under maxBytes (body-less path)\n ✓ readResponseBodySnippet > truncates by maxBytes in the body-less path\n ✓ readResponseBodySnippet > enforces maxBytes before maxChars in the body-less path\n ✓ readResponseBodySnippet > does not split multi-byte UTF-8 characters at the byte boundary\n ✓ readResponseBodySnippet > stream path still enforces maxBytes\n ✓ readResponseBodySnippet > stream path still enforces maxChars\n ✓ readResponseBodySnippet > returns empty string when maxBytes is 0 (body-less path)\n ✓ readResponseBodySnippet > returns empty string for empty response body\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  9 passed (9)\n```\n\nhttp-body tests also pass: 13/13 (readResponsePrefix export has no side effects)\n\n**What was not tested:** Full end-to-end Gateway error handling -- only the `readResponseBodySnippet()` function was verified via direct unit test.\n\n## Changes\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/infra/http-body.ts:189` | Export `readResponsePrefix` (was private function) |\n| `src/infra/http-error-body.ts:1,10` | Import `readResponsePrefix`, replace unbounded `response.text()` with bounded `readResponsePrefix` |\n| `src/infra/http-error-body.test.ts` | Add `arrayBuffer()` to mock; update multi-byte boundary test expectation |\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- **merge-risk: Low** -- bounded read is strictly safer; streaming path unchanged\n- **User-visible behavior change?** No -- same limits, same truncation behavior\n- **Config/env/migration change?** No\n- **Security/auth/network change?** No\n",
